didn't want the students to hear him, \"Has she ever gone camping before?\" [345] \"No, it's her first time,\" Takakura said with a smile. \"She seems very excited...\"\n[346] \"Ah, I can see that she is very excited\u2026\" Y\u016btani winked at Takeyama. [347] 2\n[348] The returning boat skillfully docked at the pier. It was a small boat about five meters long, with a canopy over the cockpit and a tent at the back. Y\u016btani had only seen boats like this with open decks in Hanoi and Istanbul. [349] \"Excuse me, are you Mr. Y\u016btani?\" A man approached Y\u016btani with a warm smile. [350] \"Yes, I am.\" [351] \"I am from the Shigemura Research Institute, my name is Yamane.\" The man nodded slightly. \"Is that Miss Nishiyama?\" [352] \"No, it's not me.\" The exchange student, Xiao Wu, answered quickly. [353] \"Miss Nishiyama is over there...\" Sugawara pointed to the girl with an umbrella buying juice from the vending machine. \"I'm sorry for the trouble. It's really nice of you to come all the way here.\" [354] \"No problem.\" Yamane shook his head. \"The director asked me to guide you, so I came. It's the first time we've had so many guests on the island. If you don't mind, how about a small welcome party tomorrow night...?\" [355] \"Is the campsite close to the research institute?\" Sugawara asked as he walked. The students had already boarded the boat. [356] \"The island is small, and the research institute and the campsite are at the two ends of the island. Well... it takes about ten minutes to walk there, of course we also have cars...\"\n[357] Yamane seems to be a little older than Xucun. He doesn't look like an office worker, wearing a T-shirt and jeans, with messy hair and a beard that hasn't been shaved for a few days. After getting on the boat, Yamane handed Xucun a business card. His name is Yamane Yashin, and his position is Vice President of the Shinagawa Research Institute. Xucun was a little surprised. [358] \"How many employees does the Shinagawa Research Institute have?\" Xucun didn't bring his own business card. [359] \"About fifty people fixed.\" Yamane sat on the bench of the small boat. [360] West Garden is the last to board the boat. She folded her umbrella and came to Xucun's side. [361] \"Miharu, this is Shigemura-san, the Deputy Director of the research institute.\" Kusaka introduced Miharu to Shigemura. [362] \"Hello.\" Miharu quickly bowed. [363] \"You visited a month ago,\" Shigemura said with a smile to Miharu. \"I was out of town and didn't see you. I heard you are the old friend of the director\u2026\"\n[364] \"So, you mean the fourth power of an old friend,\" Miharu smiled, tilting her head slightly. \"He asked me to visit Dr. Nishikawa Harumi.\" [365] \"Ah, that's rare,\" Shigemura said. \"I also watched the video of your conversation with Dr. Nishikawa, and it was a very meaningful conversation.\" [366] \"W\u01d2 h\u00e1i r\u00e1n w\u00e9i sh\u00ec s\u012b r\u00e9n sh\u00ec j\u00ecng li\u00e0ng ne.\" M\u00e9ng hu\u00ec b\u00f9 h\u01ceo y\u00ec de d\u012b xi\u00e0 le t\u00f3u. [367] \"B\u00f9 sh\u00ec de\u2026\" T\u0101 t\u0101 ch\u016b le sh\u01d2u ju\u00e0n sh\u00ec le t\u00f3u ti\u00e1o de h\u00e0n, \"W\u01d2 z\u00e0i y\u00e1nji\u00f9 su\u01d2 l\u01d0 y\u01d0 sh\u00ed w\u01d4 ni\u00e1n le, h\u00e1i y\u012b c\u00ec b\u00f9 d\u0101ng y\u01d4 t\u0101 zh\u00ed zh\u00ed shu\u014d hu\u00e0 ne. Y\u01d2u hu\u00e0 de sh\u00ed h\u00f2u d\u00e0n d\u014du t\u014dng gu\u00f2 hu\u00e0 m\u01d2u hu\u00f2 p\u00edng k\u0101n shu\u014d, t\u00e1n hu\u00e0 n\u00e8i d\u00ecng yu\u00e1n w\u00e8i qu\u00e1n su\u01d2 k\u0101i p\u01d0ng. [368] \"B\u00f3shi shu\u00ed y\u011b ji\u00e0n ma?\" M\u00e9ng hu\u00ec w\u00e8n, \"Zh\u0113n de shu\u00ed y\u011b ji\u00e0n ma?\" [369] \"Shu\u00ed y\u011b ji\u00e0n.\" \"M\u00e9n k\u01d2u ch\u00f9 de ti\u011b b\u00e0ng f\u00e0ng xi\u00e0 le, di\u00e0n b\u014d sh\u0113ng d\u00e0 le q\u01d0 l\u00e1i. Sh\u00e0ng chu\u00e1n de zh\u01d0 y\u01d2u x\u012b chu\u0101n t\u0101 men sh\u00ed y\u012b g\u00e8 r\u00e9n h\u00e9 sh\u0101n g\u0113n. Chu\u00e1n yu\u00e1n zh\u01d0 y\u01d2u li\u01ceng g\u00e8. Xi\u01ceo chu\u00e1n m\u00e0n m\u00e0n de hu\u00ed h\u00f2u, su\u00ec xi\u00e0ng h\u00e9 xi\u00e0 y\u00f3u. S\u00f9 d\u00f9 m\u00e0n de r\u00e0ng r\u00e9n j\u012bng y\u00e0o, zh\u014dng sh\u00ed j\u01d0n j\u01d0ng j\u01d0ng r\u00e1o r\u00e1o sh\u00ec de. H\u00e9 c\u00ed li\u01ceng bi\u0101n de g\u0101ng j\u012bng m\u00e9ng y\u00f9n d\u012b b\u00e0n g\u0101o le, k\u00e0n b\u00fa ji\u00e0n su\u01d2 w\u00e9i de j\u01d0ng z\u01d0. Qi\u00e1n mi\u00e0n y\u01d2u li\u01ceng zu\u00f2 qi\u00e1o, y\u00e0o ch\u016b h\u01cei de hu\u00e0 xi\u016b y\u00e0o t\u00f3ng y\u00fa n\u00e0 xi\u00e0 mi\u00e0n t\u014dng gu\u00f2. Chu\u00e1n k\u0101i d\u00f2ng q\u01d0 l\u00e1i ji\u00f9 y\u01d2u le di\u01cen f\u0113ng, du\u014d sh\u01ceo h\u01ceo sh\u00f2u y\u012b xi\u0113 y\u012b xi\u0113. [370] \"Sh\u00ec de, w\u01d2 z\u00e0i y\u00e1nji\u00f9 su\u01d2 l\u01d0 y\u01d0 sh\u00ed w\u01d4 ni\u00e1n le, h\u00e1i\n[371] \"I heard it takes forty minutes to get to the island of Princess True Love,\" said Momo-chan. \"I thought it was far, but the boat is moving so slowly.\" [372] \"How many trips does the boat make a day?\" asked Shiroi. [373] \"It's not fixed. This boat goes to the island of Koya, not Princess True Love. It makes eight round trips a day, and we can be dropped off at Princess True Love in the middle. But if we want to board the boat from the island, we have to call them in advance.\" [374] The boat continued to sail down the river. As it passed under the concrete and steel bridge, the river finally opened up a bit. The students leaned over the railing, looking forward. Only Shiroi and Yamanaka were sitting. [375] Momo-chan had somehow managed to strike up a conversation with the crew in the open cockpit. [376] \"I'm sorry... you're so young and already an assistant director?\" Sugawara expressed his curiosity. [377] \"Yes, I was appointed last year. We retire at age forty. I'm the oldest in the research institute besides the director.\" [378] \"Wow, you retire at forty? What happens then?\" Sugawara was puzzled. [379] \"We get a pension, which is quite substantial. It lasts for a while. After that, if we want, we can go back to work. With our experience, there are plenty of job opportunities.\" [380] \"That's impressive,\" Sugawara nodded vigorously. \"That shows high levels of ability. If only universities were like that...\"\n[381] The slow boat they were on finally reached the other side of the estuary and left the dam. The waves on the sea became slightly larger, but the weather was sunny, there was no wind, and the sea was still calm. Several small fishing boats floated on the sea, and young people riding on single-person motorboats could still be seen in the distance. The boat was heading south towards the high-hanging sun. [382] M\u00e9ngr\u00ecn walked towards Shuzhuang and Shengen from the cockpit. [383] \"Can I ask you about Dr. Shinobu Akagi?\" M\u00e9ngr\u00ecn asked Shengen, \"About Dr. Akagi killing her parents...\"\n[384] \"West Garden, don't be so impolite.\" Shuzhuang said. [385] \"No, it's okay. It's not something that needs to be particularly concealed.\" Shengen smiled bitterly, \"Don't take it to heart... We don't have much common sense about etiquette... You can see my appearance.\" [386] Indeed. The deputy director came out to greet the guests without tying his tie and shaving his beard. Sugawa thought that the employees of the research institute on the isolated island were a group of superhumans. [387] \"Do you know about the incident fifteen years ago?\" Mio asked. [388] \"No, I don't. I went there after that,\" Yamanaka answered. \"So I haven't met Dr. Shinobu Momiji Left-san, and I haven't met Dr. Shinobu Momiji Mei-chan either.\" [389] \"What happened?\" Mio's delicate wrist rested on the back of the bench. [390] \"What happened?\" Yamanaka looked puzzled. [391] \"She loves to hear such things. It's not a good hobby,\" Shin'en said, lighting a cigarette. \"She just reads murder novels.\" [392] \"They are mystery novels,\" Mizuho corrected. [393] \"As far as I know... the incident happened at the research institute, right?\" Shin'en asked Shin'en. [394] \"Yes, it was when the research institute was being built halfway. The island wasn't a private property yet. At that time, Ms. Akira Mizuhara was fourteen years old. However, as a child prodigy, she was famous not only in the field of computers but also throughout the country. I went to work at the research institute because I admired her. She killed her parents, Dr. Akira Mizuhara and Dr. Mei Chien Mizuhara, with a knife in her own room.\" Shin'en spoke without emotion. [395] \"Were there any witnesses at the time?\" Mizuho asked immediately. [396] \"Yeah, she was caught by Ms. Akita's uncle... the current director... at the crime scene. The director's wife also saw it. I heard it directly from the director.\" [397] \"A 14-year-old girl killed two people without any interference?\" Maki asked. [398] \"I don't know,\" Mountain shook his head. [399] \"She told me... her doll killed her parents. What does that mean?\" Maki recalled what Ms. Akita said. [400] \"Ah, I know that too. Ms. Akita has multiple personalities.\" Mountain answered casually. [401] \"I've heard a little about it.\" Kurosu agreed. [402] \"I always feel like I don't quite understand... but the treating doctor said so, and the court acquitted her. You can understand it by talking to her. I thought it was a joke at first.\" [403] \"How did you know?\" Momo straightened up. [404] \"When I met Ms. Nishiyama, she said she was Ms. Matsutani Shiki...\" Yamane wiped the sweat off his forehead, \"uh...yeah.\" [405] \"Hmm, yes, she said that herself.\" Momo answered. [406] \"Sayuri Higashida sometimes speaks like a man,\" Yamamoto explained. \"When you ask her again, she'll say her name is Kazuo. Everyone at the lab knows. I watched the video too. She said the killer was a doll... not another personality, right?\" [407] \"Why did she say 'doll'?\" asked Mouri. \"Do you mean a personality like a doll?\" [408] \"No, just a figment of my imagination,\" Yamamoto smiled. \"Anyway, any personality she has is top-notch in terms of work. She's a genius in programming. Her talents remain intact. It was Sayuri Higashida, Ph.D., who made the Higashida Research Institute what it is today. Our work relies entirely on her guidance. She'll tell you anything if you ask her.\" [409] \"So, where is Sayuri Higashida Ph.D. in the lab? Is she really on the island?\" Mouri asked an odd question. [410] \"Ha, yes, that's understandable,\" Yamamoto laughed in response. \"Indeed, you can only see her on TV. But she's actually in a certain place underground in the lab. Her living quarters are on the west side of the second floor underground, taking up about a quarter of that floor. That's around six rooms... maybe it's more accurate to say she's been isolated since that incident. There's only one door, always under strict surveillance. Sayuri Higashida hasn't left that place in fifteen years. Well, the lab itself is a bit strange too... no windows at all. We work almost like her in a sealed environment.\" [411] \"Secret room\" was a new term for Kamata. [412] \"Who can enter Dr. Akagi's place?\" Mizuki asked. [413] \"No one can,\" Nagano said. \"After the murder incident, no one from the outside could, and no one in the lab could meet her directly. Moreover, Dr. Akagi herself refuses to meet anyone. As far as I know... she's completely cut off from the outside world. The network is monitored, and sending personal emails doesn't work. Sending her things personally is also not allowed.\" [414] \"That's to prevent any leaks of secrets, I guess,\" Kamata said, taking a drag of his cigarette. [415] \"There's that aspect to it, too,\" Nagano answered. \"Meeting with Dr. Akagi cannot be done in a private setting. We need several people to monitor and record the interaction. Dr. Akagi's talents are the property of the entire research institute.\" [416] \"So, she is the main program,\" Hidaka said. [417] \"Yes... that's right. It's running smoothly now,\" Mountai said, lighting a cigarette. \"Perhaps she wishes to live like a machine... ah, I'm sorry, I didn't mean to say that.\" [418] \"What is Dr. Makoto's current research topic?\" Hidaka asked, extinguishing his cigarette in the ashtray. [419] \"That information is classified,\" Mountai said with a smile. \"I'm sorry, but I cannot disclose that to you. It's the highest secret in the lab.\" [420] \"Indeed...,\" Hidaka said, smiling. \"If the murder incident can be made public, why can't that be?\" [421] \"Haha... Not reasonable, is it?\" Shigemura smiled and said, \"We are all unreasonable people. We... all the staff except the director and the chief doctor are not married. We live in the lab, get up and work, and the same goes for morning and evening... There is no such thing as working hours. The salary is three times that of ordinary employees... but there is no opportunity to spend money, just depositing it into the bank. Almost everyone works alone, with very few opportunities to meet people. Meetings are held electronically, and communication is through computers. We casually say bad things about each other without any etiquette. We don't greet each other or work together. There are no welcome parties or farewell parties. No company tours. The only rule is to keep your mouth shut until you finish a task.\" [422] \"An ideal workplace,\" Sugawara smiled. [423] 3\n[424] The sea color was between blue and green. A concrete pier floated in the small harbor of the island. There were no other boats in the dam except for them. After everyone disembarked, the boat immediately reversed and turned around. When Sugawara and the others disembarked, the boat was slowly leaving the dam. [425] The ferry terminal had nothing but an empty small waiting room. There was a faded sign for tourism, but it was no longer legible. Next to the sign, there was a four-wheel drive car parked on a grassy, overgrown patch of land. [426] \"It's about a fifteen-minute walk from here to the campsite. Please put the heavy luggage on top of the car. I can only carry four people besides me. S\u014dma-sensei and\u2026 ah, two ladies\u2026 let's prioritize the ladies and send them first.\" The two ladies referred to were Nishimura Momiji and the exchange student Xiao Wu. [427] \"And one more person,\" S\u014dma pointed to Kuni, \"I forgot to introduce her. She is my assistant Kuni-san. She is the most skilled in designing programs among us, and I am second\u2026\"\n[428] A tall woman with a straw hat, Kuni-sono, approached. She was not wearing makeup, and her head was shaved very short. Her tall stature made it difficult to recognize her as a woman. [429] \"I'll walk there,\" Kuni said reluctantly. However, she was always reluctant, and it may not be because she was in a bad mood.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 2:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:35 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nThis includes New Vine Director and Miss Futaba, and there are exactly fifty people who are still alive now. I have confirmed all fifty people.\" [1561] The questioning continues for about an hour when suddenly the electronic bell rings, and another interface appears on the screen. [1562] I am Tomoko Shima. [1563] Vice President, I remember something. I had an appointment with a reporter from a women's magazine tomorrow at 1 pm. She is coming to our island to gather material. [1564] \"Thank goodness!\" After reading this, Professor Saito breathes a sigh of relief. [1565] Mr. Yamanaka turns to look at Professor Saito. \"That's right. We can contact the outside world as soon as we send anyone to the port.\" [1566] \"So, there won't be any ships coming today, right?\" Mizuki asked. \"Who should we send to the port?\" [1567] \"No, there was no prior contact, so who would happen to come to the island? The chances are almost zero... We have to hold out for another day... The police won't come before tomorrow afternoon.\" [1568] Sugawara replied to Itoh Fujiko's email, keeping it simple: I know. [1569] At around 7 o'clock, the morning meeting ended. Finally, Sugawara notified all the staff that they would hold another full-staff electronic meeting in four hours. [1570] Sugawara extinguished the cigarette, and Mizuki asked, \"Can't we know who we're talking to through this electronic meeting?\" [1571] Yamauchi: \"No, everything is recorded. We just used anonymous login this time. Compared to face-to-face meetings, this form saves time. It eliminates a lot of unnecessary chatter... And there's no room in the research institute that can accommodate more than fifty people.\" [1572] Shimizu: \"You've already conveyed the news of the director's passing, right?\" [1573] Yamauchi: \"It may be spread soon. I never intended to keep it a secret.\" [1574] Fuyu: \"The killer might have been listening to today's meeting.\" [1575] Yamauchi: \"Yeah, what should we do? I'm hungry. The teachers are too... Can we have some toast?\" [1576] \"I'll have some too,\" said Kimihiko, nodding lightly. [1577] \"Is that so, Miss Saotome?\" The head of the department glances at Akagi. [1578] Akagi doesn't respond, her eyes fixed on the racing car on the table. [1579] \"Miss Saotome,\" Kimihiko gently taps Akagi's shoulder. [1580] \"Excuse me\u2026\" Akagi looks bewildered. \"The door inside Dr. True's residence\u2026 the aluminum door\u2026 was it always open? How was it controlled?\" [1581] Yamanaka smiled and said, \"Ah, you mean that door. It is controlled by our research institute's Deborah Management System (Deborah: Iranian prophet, named after her. - Translator's note). Only authorized people can open it from the outside, and it can also be opened from Dr. Akagi's room. However, only Dr. Akagi can open it in her room. Dr. Akagi held out her hand...\"\n[1582] Yamanaka suddenly stopped talking. His expression suddenly froze. [1583] Hidaka slowly said to Mai, \"I also thought so.\" [1584] \"Eh? You noticed it too, teacher!\" Mai exclaimed. [1585] \"I denied this inference because it made sense,\" Hidaka slowly said, \"that's reasonable.\" [1586] Momiji said, \"To open that door, you need Dr. Akutagawa's right hand... So, was it to cover something?\" [1587] \"The killer opened the door with the right hand of Dr. Akutagawa, who was cut off?\" The mountain root finally spoke, \"I can't believe it. Is it really for this?\" [1588] Kamitani said, \"No, it's not just that door\u2026\"\n[1589] \"Walking around the research institute with Dr. Akutagawa's right hand?\" [1590] Kamitani nodded and said, \"Or\u2026\"\n[1591] \"That's incredible\u2026\" Minghui exclaimed, her eyes wide and mouth agape. [1592] \"Yes, it's incredible,\" Xiangchuan replied. [1593] \"So, you cut off Dr. Akagi's hand just to open the door? Is that necessary?\" Minghui asked. \"Anyone in the research institute could open the door.\" [1594] \"No, not anywhere,\" Shigaraki answered. \"For example, the door to my room, only the owner can open it. In other places, only those with permission to use it, or those who have logged in, can open the door. For instance, to get to the rooftop where the alligator's helicopter is parked, you have to go through an exit, and that exit can only be opened by the director, the director's wife, and me. The control room where everyone was just now isn't accessible to everyone either.\" [1595] \"Where can you open with Dr. Akagi's right hand?\" Minghui asked. [1596] The mountain root replied, \"I'm not sure. She doesn't seem to have logged in anywhere. But the aluminum door to the exit of Ms. Shinagawa's room is the only one she can open.\" [1597] \"What about the main entrance of the research institute?\" [1598] \"Anyone can come and go through the main entrance. However, according to my investigation, no one has left.\" [1599] The girl whispered, \"It's really incredible. Why did you cut off her feet?\" [1600] \"Indeed, there are too many incredible things,\" said the mountain root. [1601] \"How did the killer get into that room? And how did he get out? And when did it happen? There are guards stationed outside the room 24 hours a day, and the surveillance cameras are monitoring everything. And the surveillance system is completely independent of 'Red Magic.' Even if the system is attacked by a virus and abnormalities occur, the surveillance system will not be affected at all... It seems that there are too many incredible things.\" [1602] Nakanishi nodded. \"Indeed, as you said, Professor. I find the abnormality of 'Red Magic' the most incredible. It can't send emails and the phone can't be used. And... We used the Deborah Management System of the research institute to open the yellow door of Ms. Akutagawa's room, and the lights were flashing. Other than that, there have been no other abnormalities. It seems that the killer must have tampered with the program to implement this murder plan, but it was not a virus attack. If that's the case, why is there no evidence of altering the program? I can't understand... First of all, only a few people in the institute could have done all this. That is, the people who have access to the system. Water Valley, Island Field... Me. Ms. Akutagawa herself couldn't do it. She couldn't reach the system from her room.\" [1603] Mugi added, \"The traces of opening the roof door have disappeared. When the director was killed, someone must have opened that door. But there was no record at the time. Were the records deleted?\" [1604] \"No... That's impossible. Changing the program and writing some specific data into it is possible, but if that's the case, there will be traces of program changes.\" [1605] \"Why can't the records be changed? In the program, so-called change traces are also data, right? Changing these data should be possible, shouldn't it?\" Mugi continued to ask. [1606] \"That's not possible, Miss Yozugawa. In general UNIX, it is possible, but 'Red Magic' has always had very strong security. As a result, there is no need to modify files that do not need to be modified. Even the user of the file cannot do it. In 'Red Magic', there is a file attribute that is read-only and can never be modified. This is different from general data files. The record file has this attribute.\" [1607] \"So, it's not that the data was deleted, but that it was never recorded from the beginning,\" Naito said. \"Only a few specific people can do this, and the program will not record them.\" [1608] \"No, besides that, the program must be rewritten,\" Shingae replied. [1609] \"Ah, I don't understand at all,\" Momo sighed. [1610] \"Well, let's eat first,\" Shingae smiled and went to the kitchen. [1611] Fujisawa glanced at his watch. It was already 7:00 am. He yawned widely. Moriguchi leaned back in his chair and closed his eyes. [1612] 2\n[1613] Yamane's breakfast was very delicious. There didn't seem to be a cafeteria in the research institute. The staff of the institute seemed to eat in their own rooms. Yamane seemed to be very skilled in cooking. [1614] From 8:00 am, Yamane, Mizuki, Kagura, and New Vine seemed to have a meeting. Fujisawa and Moriguchi decided to return to the campsite, and Yamane sent them to the entrance of the research institute. [1615] \"I'll lend you the car... It was originally prepared for emergencies... There's only a large truck left here besides the jeep.\" [1616] Shuai said, \"It's okay, it's okay. We may still come to visit you. What time is it convenient for you?\" [1617] Yamauchi looked at his watch and said, \"I'll send a car to pick you up after lunch. How about 2:00?\" [1618] Shuai nodded and said, \"Okay, I know.\" [1619] The red door of the research institute was lowered and closed again. Shuai and Menghui walked down the cement steps. [1620] The sun was still so intense that it seemed to burn people, but the temperature was not high. The sound of cicadas could be heard in the distance, and there was a summer scent in the air. [1621] Mishima put her hand over her forehead and said, \"Oh, I'm going to get sunburned. I didn't bring an umbrella...\"\n[1622] The two walked slowly back to the campsite. Last night it was too dark to see anything, but now they saw that the road was a straight, gently sloping path. The ground was paved with asphalt, and there were rows of wooden poles on both sides. There were no residential houses. At one point, there were a few households in the southern part of the island, near the port, but now the entire island has become the private property of the Higashitani family. [1623] They arrived at the campsite in fifteen minutes. Edogawa's assistant Kozue, the foreign student Xiao Wu, and the graduate student Hinata were sitting on a wooden stool chatting. [1624] When Edogawa and Mishima approached, Hinata asked loudly, \"Where did you go?\" [1625] \"Good morning,\" Edogawa replied. \"You asked where I went, of course to the research institute. Where are the others?\" [1626] Kousuke answered, \"They went to the beach.\" [1627] Hirano stood up and asked, \"Did you stay at the research institute? Everyone was worried.\" [1628] \"Worried? But everyone went to the beach!\" Kousuke said with a smile. [1629] Hirano seemed a little angry and said, \"I stayed behind because I was worried about you and Professor Naito.\" [1630] \"We didn't sleep all night,\" Momo said, sounding truly tired. \"We had some trouble.\" [1631] \"Well, I'm going to go take a nap there first,\" said Xucun. [1632] Mengei also crawled into the tent closest to the edge. [1633] Xucun laid down a plastic sheet under a large tree next to the tent and fell asleep with a straw hat over his face. The gentle breeze blew, so it wasn't too hot. He seemed to be sleeping soundly. [1634] However