te. This is the only way to get around the island.\" [438] \"Thank you for the trouble,\" said Mr. Awakura as he got off the van from the back. The umbrella girl and Mr. Shiozaki unloaded the luggage, and Mr. Nakajima helped them. [439] \"There's no phone here, so if you need anything, come find me at the research institute. I have some work to do and will be back later. I'll come back in the evening to bother you again...\"\n[440] The four-wheel drive van drove away down the slightly sloping road and disappeared. Suddenly, the surroundings fell silent. Although you couldn't see the sea, you could hear the sound of the waves. [441] There was a forest not far from the beach, and it was very cool under the shade of the trees. You could hear the sound of cicadas like white noise. The path leading to the campsite was a gravel road. The three of them couldn't carry the luggage that had just been unloaded from the car, so they had to wait for the other students to arrive. [442] \"This is the most difficult camping trip for the Kusaka team,\" said Kusaka as he lit a cigarette. [443] \"Difficult? Why?\" Ootani asked with a relaxed expression. She was holding an umbrella. [444] \"Ootani-san, no one comes to the campsite with an umbrella,\" said Kusaka. \"Camping is difficult. There might be centipedes around here.\" [445] \"I brought insect repellent, so it's okay,\" said Ootani. \"I brought the umbrella because I was afraid of rain, but it can also be used as a rain umbrella...\"\n[446] \"No, it's quite interesting,\" Ou smiled. She is a Chinese student who came to study in April this year. She was born in Nanjing and is known to be very heat-resistant. Today, she is dressed more suitable for camping than Wakaba. [447] \"How do you cook?\" Ou asked. \"I think cooking is the most fun. Do you use firewood?\" [448] Ou is a graduate student of Nakagawa who came to study from China in April this year. She was born in Nanjing and is known to be very heat-resistant. Today, she is 