e sounds. She often said that she liked the sound of car and motorcycle engines. Because she liked the sound of engines, her car didn't have a sound system or a radio. [494] As the night deepened, the topic naturally, or rather consciously, turned to strange stories. [495] With graduate student Tamura at the center, everyone took turns telling short stories. However, since they were all science students, they were not good at this, and the atmosphere was not lively. The most frightened was graduate student Hirose, but the three female students were not so bad. The foreign student, Xiaowu, didn't understand much Japanese, and the assistant professor, Kari, couldn't react much either, so the boys put their hopes in Yamanaka. However, they failed. There was no one who had seen a ghost or UFO, and no one believed in it. Yamanaka said that she was more afraid of difficult Chinese characters than ghosts, and everyone laughed. She said, \"The two Chinese characters I'm most afraid of are 'pinyin'.\" [496] However, there were still some people who continued to tell made-up stories until Professor Kuni said, \"Stupid, what's the point?\" [497] It was almost ten o'clock, and it seemed that Yamanaka would not come. So everyone started eating ice cream. After finishing, Akane, Xiao Wu, and Professor Kuni went to the small building of the campsite to take a bath. When they came back, most of the students had gone to the tents. [498] Kurokawa was still not sleepy. He wanted to smoke the last cigarette before going into the tent. [499] Professor Kuni and Xiao Wu went to the female students' tent. Akane put her things in the tent and then walked towards Kurokawa. Upon closer inspection, everyone else was gone except for them. [500] \"Everyone is quite observant,\" Akane sat on a log next to Kurokawa. [501] \"Just pretend I didn't hear that. Everyone was tired after a day of work,\" Sui River exhaled smoke and looked at the sky, \"So many stars. I haven't seen such a beautiful sky in fifteen years, unbelievable.\" [502] Sui River was a little surprised by his own words, as he had never seen the real Arida Shiki in his mind. [503] \"Not only Dr. Arida, but also the people in the research institute are probably watching the screen,\" Momo also looked at the sky. [504] \"But that way of life may not be bad,\" Sui River said, \"Feeling that nature is beautiful in itself is unnatural, which means life is dirty. Only by living in a place separated from nature, without windows, can one discover one's own beauty. Because of doing boring work and living a dirty life, one wants to be praised for something natural.\" [505] \"Such a scene may become virtual at any time, and people will have to appreciate it in the house,\" Momo said, \"But generally, people will have a sense of resistance...\"\n[506] \"Most people will think that nature is fake,\" Shuai Cui lit another cigarette. \"But nature is all fake. People must accept the natural made by computers. Although it's deceiving... but humans should realize that there is no real... going around criticizing the loss of humanity is nonsense. Computers are the most human-like and the most natural among the tools humans have created.\" [507] \"Teacher, can I smoke a cigarette?\" Miao Hua smiled. \"Is your 'deceiving' referring to something that's good for people?\" [508] \"I don't like the word, but yes, I guess so,\" Shuai Cui said. \"Don't smoke, you're not old enough.\" [509] Miao Hua pouted her lips. \"I'll be twenty soon.\" [510] \"When the pliers were first invented, some stubborn people said that using pliers was inhumane. They said that using such a tool was a sign of decline. Even fire, at first, some ethnic groups firmly refused. But we are a species that uses tools, and we can't go back. It is those who criticize loneliness and emptiness that have lost their humanity.\" [511] \"But isn't nuclear energy a problem?\" asked Momiji, hugging her knees. [512] \"It is a problem that the energy is too great